From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Exo names its outputs (xdg_output.name)

Exo offers zxdg_output_manager_v1 version 3 but never sent an output's
name, which the protocol has required since version 2, once and before the
first done. Qt 6 counts an output only once its name has come
(QWaylandScreen::requiredEvents), so every Qt 6 Wayland app found no
screens and ran on a placeholder ("There are no outputs - creating
placeholder screen"): Flameshot and ksnip could not take a screenshot
(found on the NVIDIA test PC, 2026-10-23, with WAYLAND_DEBUG: geometry, mode,
scale, done, logical position and size, description, no name).

The name is DISPLAY-<display id>, which stays the same for a monitor.

diff --git a/components/exo/wayland/wayland_display_observer.cc b/components/exo/wayland/wayland_display_observer.cc
index e26b833ac24d5..977603fd2599c 100644
--- a/components/exo/wayland/wayland_display_observer.cc
+++ b/components/exo/wayland/wayland_display_observer.cc
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 #include <wayland-server-protocol-core.h>
 #include <xdg-output-unstable-v1-server-protocol.h>
 
+#include "base/strings/strcat.h"
+#include "base/strings/string_number_conversions.h"
 #include "components/exo/wayland/output_metrics.h"
 #include "components/exo/wayland/server_util.h"
 #include "components/exo/wayland/wayland_display_output.h"
@@ -125,6 +127,18 @@ void WaylandDisplayHandler::OnXdgOutputCreated(
 
   xdg_output_resource_ = xdg_output_resource;
 
+  // NickelOS: the output's name, which xdg_output version 2 and later send
+  // once, before the first done. Qt 6 counts an output only once it has its
+  // name: without one, a Qt app found no screens at all (a placeholder
+  // instead; Flameshot and ksnip could not capture). Named by the display's
+  // id, which stays the same for a monitor.
+  if (wl_resource_get_version(xdg_output_resource_) >=
+      ZXDG_OUTPUT_V1_NAME_SINCE_VERSION) {
+    zxdg_output_v1_send_name(
+        xdg_output_resource_,
+        base::StrCat({"DISPLAY-", base::NumberToString(id())}).c_str());
+  }
+
   display::Display display;
   if (!display::Screen::Get()->GetDisplayWithDisplayId(id(), &display)) {
     return;
